  "scraped_at": null,
  "content": {
    "title": "Iowa basketball tops Clemson: Final score, recap, highlights",
    "text": "Updated March 20, 2026, 8:59 p.m. CTIowa (22-12, 10-10 Big Ten) has its first NCAA Tournament victory under first-year head coach Ben McCollum.Spurred on by terrific efforts from the Hawkeyes' supporting cast, Iowa fans can celebrate the program's first March Madness victory in five years. The ninth-seeded Hawkeyes downed No. 8 seed Clemson, 67-61, in the first round in the South Region.Led by 21 points off its bench and 15 points from junior guard Kael Combs, Iowa was able to overcome an off shooting night from senior point guard Bennett Stirtz. Stirtz still finished with a game-high 16 points, but it came on a 4-for-17 shooting effort.Take a look back at the Hawkeyes' NCAA Tournament win through this recap and the highlights: FINAL: Iowa 67, Clemson 61In Heaven There Is No Beer. Iowa WINS!The Hawkeyes topple Clemson and march on to the Round of 32. Iowa has its first NCAA Tournament win since 2021 and its first tourney win under head coach Ben McCollum. 13.2, 2nd Half: Iowa 65, Clemson 60As Iowa tries to ice this game away, Stirtz gets into trouble in the corner and calls timeout to avoid a turnover. Hawkeyes just need to protect the basketball and make free throws and they can make their Sunday Round of 32 plans.Iowa is now out of timeouts. Iowa challenges that the basketball touched the base lineOfficials have ruled that Iowa touched the basketball last, but that it went out of bounds and touched the base line. Upon review, it looks like Combs clearly gains possession of the basketball and that the basketball did not touch the base line.Iowa should win this challenge and have possession leading by six and with just 42.7 seconds remaining.Hawkeyes win the challenge. :56, 2nd Half: Iowa 63, Clemson 57Combs comes up with the biggest bucket of the day so far for the Hawkeyes. As the shot clock was dwindling and with Iowa leading by only four, Combs puts his head down, gets inside and finds the tough finish to give Iowa a six-point lead. Clemson challenges possession: 2:17, 2nd Half: Iowa 59, Clemson 53The call on the floor is last touched by Clemson and Iowa basketball, but the Tigers have challenged and want another look at it.After review, it is an unsuccessful challenge. 3:47, 2nd Half: Iowa 57, Clemson 51It's a tight one coming down the stretch. At the under-four, Clemson has the basketball with a 1-and-1 look trailing by just six. Iowa had opened up a 14-point lead at 54-40 when Koch was fouled on a 3-point shot with 7:32 left to play.But, Dillon Hunter, Dallas Thomas and Jestin Porter have all connected from downtown since to keep Clemson within striking distance. Tate Sage providing a spark: 7:36, 2nd Half: Iowa 51, Clemson 40Iowa needed some other Hawkeyes to step up to complement Stirtz and Banks. Sage has been awesome for Iowa in this second half, adding seven points so far off the Hawkeyes' bench. 11:57, 2nd Half: Iowa 42, Clemson 33Tate Sage with back-to-back buckets for the Hawkeyes. Big spark off the Iowa bench and the Hawkeyes are back in front by nine. 13:48, 2nd Half: Iowa 38, Clemson 33The Tigers closed to within just two points. Then, Stirtz drills his third 3-pointer of the evening. Iowa has led by as many as a dozen in this contest.Clemson has owned the points in the paint battle thus far, 18-10, and that's been a key piece in the Tigers' rally. 15:22, 2nd Half: Iowa 35, Clemson 31After an opening trey from Stirtz to start the second half, Clemson has held Iowa scoreless since. The Tigers are on a 6-0 run to tighten things in the South Region. HALFTIME: Iowa 32, Clemson 25Iowa takes a seven-point lead into the halftime break.Combs leads Iowa in scoring with 11 points at halftime. Stirtz is just 2-of-8 shooting (1-of-5 from 3-point distance) at the break but he does have eight points. Banks has six points and both Folgueiras and Cooper Koch have knocked down 3-pointers and have three points at the break.Iowa is shooting 42% from the field (10-of-24) and 33% from 3-point range (5-of-15). Clemson is shooting 37% from the field (10-of-27) and 36% from beyond the arc (4-of-11).Iowa is winning the battle on the boards, 18-13. Kael Combs' big day continues: Iowa 25, Clemson 16With 3:44 left until halftime, Combs continues to add to a fast start. Combs is leading the Hawkeyes with 11 points on a perfect 4-for-4 shooting start.Combs' season-high is 18 points against Nebraska earlier this month on March 8. Bennett Stirtz is getting help: Iowa 22, Clemson 12Combs has provided some first-half help for Stirtz. And Banks has as well. Right now, Iowa's defense is suffocating Clemson for the most part.Iowa leads by 10 at the under-8 timeout. There's 7:03 left until halftime. 8:15, 1st Half: Iowa 22, Clemson 10Stirtz splits the defense and gets inside for his second bucket.Iowa is limiting Clemson to 4-of-19 shooting (21%) and just 1-of-6 (17%) from 3-point distance. Meanwhile, Iowa is shooting 53% from the field (8-of-15) and 4-of-9 (44%) from 3-point land.Combs has eight points, Tavion Banks has six and Stirtz has five to lead the Hawkeyes. 11:32, 1st Half: Iowa 18, Clemson 8It's a strong start for the Hawkeyes. Iowa has opened an early double-figure lead in Florida over Clemson.Off a nifty behind-the-back assist from Stirtz, Alvaro Folgueiras becomes the third Hawkeye to hit from deep. 15:49, 1st Half: Iowa 8, Clemson 3Iowa and Clemson are underway in Tampa. Bennett Stirtz splashes his first 3-pointer of the day and his first points of the day to give the Hawkeyes an early five-point lead at the under-16 timeout.Kael Combs beat the shot clock to give Iowa its first points of the day. Iowa vs. Clemson injury reportThere's no major developments on the injury front for Iowa going in, but Clemson is without its second-leading scorer and leading rebounder. Carter Welling suffered a torn ACL during Clemson's ACC Tournament run. Where to watch Iowa basketball vs. Clemson in March MadnessWatch Iowa vs. ClemsonTV: TNTTipoff time: 5:50 p.m. CTLive stream: Watch on Sling (Regional restrictions may apply)Contact/Follow us @HawkeyesWire on X (formerly Twitter) and like our page on Facebook to follow ongoing coverage of Iowa news, notes and opinions. Follow Josh on X: @JoshOnHawks",
